From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:35:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Food history with charts, and Day / Week / Month
 calendar in "My day"

- Food tab gets Today / History: range 7 / 30 / 90 days, averages (kcal,
  balance, protein; today left out), eaten-vs-burned bars with the goal
  line, stacked macros, and average kcal by meal. The real-burn card and
  previous days move into History. Burn comes from FoodEnergy.loadRange
  (three reads for the whole range, also used by the coach and the
  adaptive estimate instead of one load per day).
- "My day" switches Day / Week / Month (remembered), with previous/next and
  a way back to today. Week lists each day that has events or tasks;
  Month is a Monday-first grid with a dot for events and one for tasks,
  and the tapped day's list below. DayAgendaSource.range buckets events on
  every day they touch; Google Tasks keeps every open task and each view
  picks its days (overdue ones only on today).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
